<section class="card" id="preface">
<h2>Preface</h2>
<p>This work is intended to stimulate the interest of Chamba people in learning about their history, culture and language, especially Chamba people living outside their traditional communities. It is a contribution toward sharing knowledge and encouraging younger generations to learn, preserve and pass on the Chamba language and culture.</p>
<p>Language is an important part of identity. This book introduces Chamba names and their meanings, Chamba alphabets, numerals, months, days, body parts, common words and cultural objects. It also recognizes Chamba communities including Dakka, Ganye, Kungana, Tongo and Chamba communities in Cameroon and Togo.</p>
<p>Preserving our language is a collective responsibility. I hope this material will encourage families, students and Chamba people everywhere to learn and teach the language.</p>
</section>

<section class="card" id="dedication">
<h2>Dedication</h2>
<p>This work is dedicated to the memory of my late father, <b>Dr. SANI SHUAIBU JATAU</b>, and my mother, <b>HAUWA'U BALA ABDULLAH</b>.</p>
<p>It is also dedicated to my late sisters, <b>ABIDA SHUAIBU SANI</b> and <b>ARIFAT SHUAIBU SANI</b>, and to Chamba people around the world.</p>
</section>

